   "note": "Designed a translation-invariant ansatz block to exploit the cyclic symmetry of the graph connectivity problem. The block consists of uniform single-qubit rotations (RY, RZ) and a cyclic ladder of CNOTs (0-1, 1-2, ..., 5-0). This structure is invariant under cyclic permutations of the qubits (generator [1,2,3,4,5,0]), which corresponds to relabeling the nodes in a cycle. Since the feature map encodes pairwise connections, and the readout uses symmetric observables (Z_i, Z_iZ_j), this symmetry reduction significantly constrains the hypothesis space, potentially improving generalization and reducing overfitting compared to fully asymmetric blocks. The two layers of CNOTs allow for entanglement propagation across the entire ring, capturing global connectivity properties like cycles or cuts.",
